---
// Manifesto: site.md §2, copy verbatim. The /review style (Site.astro): the label on the left, the principles down the
// right with their numbers hanging, as on the home page; wide space between them (design notes: 200–300px on desktop).
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site title="Manifesto" description="Five principles I work by." image="/review-og.png">
  <main class="page manifesto">
    <section class="row intro">
      <h1 class="label caps">MANIFESTO</h1>
      <p class="title">Five principles I work&nbsp;by.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
      <span class="label" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="principles">
        <article>
          <h2><span>01.</span> Every decision has an&nbsp;author.</h2>
          <p>If no one will defend it, it shouldn't ship. Every product is built on a few thousand small decisions: what the cancel button says, where the password strength meter sits, whether the empty state is funny or quiet. Most of those get made by accident. I make them on&nbsp;purpose.</p>
          <p>Settings are unfinished decisions. So is sending people to support for something the screen could have told them. "Make it customizable" is what designers say when they can't&nbsp;decide.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2><span>02.</span> The brief is wrong until proven&nbsp;right.</h2>
          <p>A brief is the founder's first guess at the problem. The work starts with checking that guess. If you hand me a brief and I do exactly what it says, I'm not designing. I'm&nbsp;typing.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2><span>03.</span> Make the call, then check&nbsp;it.</h2>
          <p>Research sharpens a decision. It doesn't replace one. I decide from what I've seen, and research where I'm&nbsp;unsure.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2><span>04.</span> Character is not a&nbsp;layer.</h2>
          <p>A product has one voice or none. The voice shows up in places people don't think of as design: the wording on a 404, the timing of a toast notification, what your invoice email feels like. If those don't match the rest of the product, the product doesn't have a voice. It has a&nbsp;styleguide.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2><span>05.</span> The safe version is already&nbsp;taken.</h2>
          <p>Every category has its safe version, and it's already taken. The banking app in navy blue. The pharmacy site that opens with a sale. Building another one puts you at the back of a line someone else started. You should be able to tell whose product it is without seeing the&nbsp;logo.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
      <span class="label" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="end">
        <hr class="rule" />
        <div class="closing">
          <p>If this sounds like how you want to build —</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/review/" data-gem>Send a link, get a video review <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: 40px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.6vw, 80px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.058em;
  }

  .principles {
    display: grid;
    gap: 200px;
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  article {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  /* The number hangs in its own column, so a title that wraps stays under its words, and the text below lines up with
     the words, not the number. */
  h2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 38px minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: baseline;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  h2 span {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    letter-spacing: 0;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  article p {
    margin: 0 0 0 38px;
    max-width: 31em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .end {
    display: grid;
    gap: 64px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .principles {
      gap: 112px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro {
      padding-top: 16px;
    }
    .title {
      font-size: 36px;
    }
    h2 {
      grid-template-columns: 30px minmax(0, 1fr);
      font-size: 24px;
    }
    article p {
      margin-left: 30px;
    }
    .principles {
      gap: 88px;
    }
    .end {
      gap: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>
